" [:option {:value "158164"} "Coxed Pairs, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "158181"} "Coxless Fours, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "158200"} "Coxed Fours, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "158218"} "Eights, Men"]] [:script {} "$('#same_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#same_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:form {:class "form-inline form-inline-header"} [:select {:name "id", :id "other_games_select", :class "form-control"} [:option {:value ""} "In other Games"] "\n" [:option {:value "9031206"} "1896"] "\n" [:option {:value "157529"} "1904"] "\n" [:option {:value "157643"} "1920"] "\n" [:option {:value "157679"} "1924"] "\n" [:option {:value "157752"} "1928"] "\n" [:option {:value "157889"} "1932"] "\n" [:option {:value "157941"} "1936"] "\n" [:option {:value "158011"} "1948"] "\n" [:option {:value "158247"} "1956"] "\n" [:option {:value "158322"} "1960"] "\n" [:option {:value "158403"} "1964"] "\n" [:option {:value "158482"} "1968"] "\n" [:option {:value "158562"} "1972"] "\n" [:option {:value "158659"} "1976"] "\n" [:option {:value "158793"} "1980"] "\n" [:option {:value "158914"} "1984"] "\n" [:option {:value "159028"} "1988"] "\n" [:option {:value "159183"} "1992"] "\n" [:option {:value "159368"} "1996"] "\n" [:option {:value "159563"} "2000"] "\n" [:option {:value "159743"} "2004"] "\n" [:option {:value "260980"} "2008"] "\n" [:option {:value "319027"} "2012"] "\n" [:option {:value "353953"} "2016"] "\n" [:option {:value "19008433"} "2020"] "\n" [:option {:value "2012433"} "2024"]] [:script {} "$('#other_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#other_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:a {:href "/event_names/379"} "Event type"]] [:h1 {:class "event_title"} "Double Sculls, Men" [:small {} [:a {:class "footnote", :href "#", :title "Originally scheduled for Taivallahti.", :data-toggle "tooltip", :data-placement "right"} "1"]]] [:table {:class "biodata"} [:tbody {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Date"] [:td {} "20 – 23 July 1952"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Status"] [:td {} "Olympic"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Location"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/391"} "Meilahti, Helsinki"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Participants"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/events/158130"} "32 from 16 countries"]]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "Britain had replaced the United States as the world power in double sculls, but sent the relatively unheralded " [:a {:href "/athletes/37386"} "John MacMillan"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/37230"} "Peter Brandt"] " of the Cambridge University Boat Club and were not considered strong favorites. Perhaps better positioned were Denmark’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/36574"} "Ebbe Parsner"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/36542"} "Aage Larsen"] ", the defending silver medalists and two-time European Champions and Double Sculls Challenge Cup winners (1949 and 1950). Also thought to be in contention were " [:a {:href "/athletes/39816"} "Peter Stebler"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/39751"} "Emil Knecht"] " of Switzerland, the reigning European Champions, and " [:a {:href "/athletes/35695"} "Robert George"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/35760"} "Jos Van Stichel"] " of Belgium, the 1952 winners of the Double Sculls Challenge Cup at the Henley Royal Regatta. None of these men, however, would win a medal in Helsinki."] "\n\n" [:p {} "The Swiss, Britons, and Danes all found themselves eliminated by the conclusion of the opening’s round repêchage. The Belgians followed by the end of the semi-final round, leaving five lesser-known duos to contest the final. Of them, " [:a {:href "/athletes/37027"} "Jacques Maillet"] " of France was probably the best known, having been one half of the 1949 European bronze medalists. He and his new partner " [:a {:href "/athletes/36967"} "Achille Giovannoni"] ", however, would not see the podium and remained far from contention throughout the race, besting only the Czechoslovakian pairing of " [:a {:href "/athletes/40027"} "Antonín Malinkovič"] " and " [:a {:href ""} "Jiří Vykoukal"] ". It was the Argentines, " [:a {:href "/athletes/35200"} "Tranquilo Capozzo"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/35230"} "Eduardo Guerrero"] ", who dominated the field, taking the gold medal over six seconds ahead of their nearest challengers, " [:a {:href "/athletes/40402"} "Heorhiy Zhylin"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/40268"} "Ihor Yemchuk"] " of the Soviet Union. Uruguay’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/40429"} "Miguel Seijas"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/40427"} "Juan Rodríguez"] " came in third. Little did Capozzo, who had been eliminated in the semi-finals of the single sculls in 1948, and Guerrero know that they would have to savour their victory for many decades to come: Argentina would not take home another Olympic gold medal in any sport until 2004. It was the nation’s second Olympic rowing medal, and first gold, after " [:a {:href "/athletes/35273"} "Horacio Podestá"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/35205"} "Julio Curatella’s"] " third-place finish in the coxless pairs in 1936."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Pair"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/35200"} "Tranquilo Capozzo"] " / " [:a {:href "/athletes/35230"} "Eduardo Guerrero"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/ARG"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/ARG.png"}] "ARG"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/40402"} "Georgy Zhilin"] " / " [:a {:href "/athletes/40268"} "Igor Yemchuk"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/URS"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/URS.png"}] "URS"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/40429"} "Migue